# N3 example: well-formedness-error.
# Companion to well-formedness-error.srl: the source rule body
# deliberately uses a comparison before the variable it compares is
# (strictly-ordered body evaluation). N3 has no such requirement: its
# premise matcher reorders clauses by selectivity rather than evaluating
# strictly left to right (confirmed by testing), so the very same clause
# :alice a :Bad regardless.

@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#>.
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/well-formedness-error#>.

:alice :score 10.

{?score math:greaterThan 5. :alice :score ?score.} => {:alice a :Bad}.
